    {
      "id": "phrase-dejar-a-alguien--end-relationship",
      "kind": "phrase",
      "promptEs": "dejar a alguien (terminar una relación)",
      "questionEn": "How do you say that someone leaves or breaks up with a romantic partner?",
      "answerEn": "Use a form of dejar for the person ending the relationship, then identify the partner. A short word such as me or te goes before the changed form of dejar.",
      "noteEn": "With a named or stated partner, put a before that person: dejó a su pareja. With a short word, put it before dejar: me dejó, te dejo. Dejar changes for who ends the relationship and when; context separates this sense from leaving an object somewhere.",
      "example": {
        "es": "Marta dejó a su pareja.",
        "en": "Marta broke up with her partner."
      },
      "tags": [
